{"name":"Deer","hex":"#ba8759","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Deer","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Villages in Aberdeenshire, Scotland: See New Deer and Old Deer.","A township in Roseau County, Minnesota, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Deer"}],"entries":[{"title":"Deer","blocks":[{"text":"A deer or true deer is a hoofed ruminant ungulate of the family Cervidae. Cervidae is divided into subfamilies Cervinae and Capreolinae. Male deer of almost all species, as well as female reindeer, grow and shed new antlers each year. These antlers are bony extensions of the skull and are often used for combat between males."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Family_Cervidae_five_species.jpg/330px-Family_Cervidae_five_species.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deer"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Cervidae_distribution.png/500px-Cervidae_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Cervidae_distribution.png/1280px-Cervidae_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Cervidae_distribution.png/500px-Cervidae_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACervidae_distribution.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Lucas_Cranach_d.%C3%84._-_Hirschjagd_des_Kurf%C3%BCrsten_Friedrich_des_Weisen_%28Kunsthistorisches_Museum%29.jpg/500px-Lucas_Cranach_d.%C3%84._-_Hirschjagd_des_Kurf%C3%BCrsten_Friedrich_des_Weisen_%28Kunsthistorisches_Museum%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1